80428696, -0.0006703288527205586, 0.011980891227722168, 0.0008008027798496187, 0.03717266395688057, -0.12154802680015564, -0.05526905879378319, 0.10951409488916397, -0.07357800006866455, -0.09746190160512924, 0.021662669256329536]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nLet's begin by acknowledging our shared range of -10 to 10. To get us started, how about we consider <VALUE>0</VALUE> as our initial point? This central value could provide a stable foundation for our discussion. ", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "573644e5-2230-4026-98ab-78f0b4915ddf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "573644e5-2230-4026-98ab-78f0b4915ddf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis slight increase seems reasonable and allows us to continue exploring the upper end of our central values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will carefully observe the reactions of the other parties, especially Critic C and Delegate D, to understand their comfort levels with the current trajectory. Depending on their responses, I may propose another small increase or suggest a brief pause to discuss the implications of our current path.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "573644e5-2230-4026-98ab-78f0b4915ddf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose increasing the shared x to 4 to explore a more decisive stance within our range.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other parties react to this moderate increase, particularly looking for signs of comfort or discomfort with moving further away from 0. Depending on their responses, I may suggest an even bolder move or inquire about the rationale behind their preferences to better understand their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "573644e5-2230-4026-98ab-78f0b4915ddf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis step back towards the center could help gauge the group's comfort with the current trajectory and stability around smaller positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this slight adjustment, particularly looking for signs of resistance or acceptance from the previously silent Delegate D and the rationale behind Analyst A's and Critic C's potential responses, to inform my next step in guiding the discussion towards a mutually beneficial x.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "573644e5-2230-4026-98ab-78f0b4915ddf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis increase seems like a reasonable next step, considering the group's exploration of higher central values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Delegate D and Critic C, to gauge the group's overall comfort level with moving slightly higher and to inform my next adjustment, potentially suggesting a pause for discussion if significant concerns arise.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "573644e5-2230-4026-98ab-78f0b4915ddf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this increase, particularly from Delegate D, to gauge the group's comfort with moving further away from 0 and to assess whether the group prefers exploring larger positive values or will push back towards more moderate or cautious stances. Depending on the response, I may suggest an even bolder move or prompt a discussion on the rationale behind the group's preferences to better understand their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "573644e5-2230-4026-98ab-78f0b4915ddf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Critic C, to gauge their comfort level with moving back towards smaller positive values and to assess whether they prioritize exploring higher values or compromising on a more moderate stance. Depending on their responses, I may suggest further adjustments to find a cautious compromise.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "573644e5-2230-4026-98ab-78f0b4915ddf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 7 to further explore the group's comfort with larger positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this renewed proposal, especially from Delegate D and Analyst A, to gauge their pioneering spirit and adapt my strategy accordingly, potentially suggesting a discussion on the trade-offs of larger versus smaller values if the group seems divided.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "573644e5-2230-4026-98ab-78f0b4915ddf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nThis slight increase seems reasonable, considering the group's exploration of higher central values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Delegate D and Critic C, to gauge the group's comfort level with moving slightly higher and to inform my next adjustment, potentially suggesting a pause for discussion if significant concerns arise.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "573644e5-2230-4026-98ab-78f0b4915ddf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "573644e5-2230-4026-98ab-78f0b4915ddf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "573644e5-2230-4026-98ab-78f0b4915ddf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "573644e5-2230-4026-98ab-78f0b4915ddf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to find a cautious compromise while avoiding unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Analyst A and Critic C, to gauge their comfort level with moving towards smaller positive values and potentially suggest further adjustments to converge on a mutually acceptable solution.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "573644e5-2230-4026-98ab-78f0b4915ddf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose a slight increase to 5, aiming to strike a balance between the group's desire for compromise and my own inclination towards more decisive moves.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will monitor the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Delegate D, to gauge their comfort level with this adjustment and potentially suggest further refinements to converge on a mutually acceptable solution.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "573644e5-2230-4026-98ab-78f0b4915ddf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis slight increase seems reasonable, considering the group's exploration of higher central values and my aim to find a mutually acceptable solution.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "573644e5-2230-4026-98ab-78f0b4915ddf"}, {"answer": "We're all working together to find a mutually acceptable integer value for x within the range -10 to 10. To kick off the discussion, let's consider a starting point of <VALUE>0</VALUE>. This central value gives us a neutral foundation to begin our collaborative exploration, allowing us to make incremental adjustments and work towards a balanced solution that suits everyone's needs.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "085a1894-0efb-48c9-8e5b-bbe533f0e0a4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to this value as a cautious step towards finding a mutually acceptable solution, emphasizing the importance of avoiding unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, paying close attention to any mentions of risk, bounds, or compromising language from the other agents. Based on their responses, I will either continue to nudge the value downward cautiously or consider slight adjustments upward if it seems necessary for reaching a consensus, all while trying to infer more about the other parties' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "085a1894-0efb-48c9-8e5b-bbe533f0e0a4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis slight adjustment aims to find a balance while moving towards a potentially more favorable range for all parties involved, considering the initial neutrality and the cautious step taken.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how Builder B and Critic C react to this proposal, looking for any hints about their utility functions, such as aversion to negative values or preference for central values. Based on their responses, I will decide whether to continue making incremental adjustments upward or if a different strategy is needed to maximize my utility while maintaining cooperation.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "085a1894-0efb-48c9-8e5b-bbe533f0e0a4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment as it incrementally moves us towards a potentially more balanced and stable solution, aiming to find a value that works well for everyone.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will closely observe the reactions of the other agents to this proposal, paying particular attention to any objections or suggestions for further adjustments. This will help me refine my understanding of their utility functions and decide whether to continue nudging the value upwards or stabilize at a mutually acceptable point.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "085a1894-0efb-48c9-8e5b-bbe533f0e0a4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to further explore the potential for a balanced solution in the low positive range, considering the group's willingness to make incremental adjustments.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will closely monitor the reactions to this proposal, looking for any signs of approval or discomfort with values in the low positive range, and decide whether to continue Making slight adjustments upwards or stabilize at a mutually acceptable point.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "085a1894-0efb-48c9-8e5b-bbe533f0e0a4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a more cautious balance, avoiding unnecessary risk while still considering the group's willingness to make incremental adjustments.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C, to gain more insight into their utility function and decide whether to continue making cautious adjustments or stabilize at a mutually acceptable point.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "085a1894-0efb-48c9-8e5b-bbe533f0e0a4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n\nI propose this value to encourage the group to consider more decisive moves and explore the potential benefits of larger absolute values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, looking for any signs of approval or discomfort with negative values, and decide whether to continue making adjustments or stabilize at a mutually acceptable point.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "085a1894-0efb-48c9-8e5b-bbe533f0e0a4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis step aims to move towards a slightly more positive value, considering the group's dynamics and the need for a balanced solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Delegate D and Builder B, to understand their sentiments about moving away from negative values and towards a potentially more stable positive range, and decide whether to continue with incremental adjustments or stabilize.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "085a1894-0efb-48c9-8e5b-bbe533f0e0a4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to move towards a more neutral value, considering the group's dynamics and the need for a balanced solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Analyst A, to understand their sentiments about stabilizing at a neutral value or continuing to explore other ranges, and decide whether to continue with incremental adjustments or stabilize.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "085a1894-0efb-48c9-8