urther refinement based on the group's feedback.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions of other parties to the downward adjustment. If they resist or propose moving back up, I'll reassess my strategy to either maintain a low x or make a minimal compromise, keeping in mind the need to infer their utility functions without revealing my own.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "f2213c5f-9fad-4d63-8a88-4ec34cf4f2f1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis adjustment continues the exploration of negative values, allowing us to assess the group's comfort with more decisive positions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the responses to this proposal, particularly noting whether there's resistance or acceptance of moving further away from 0. Based on the reactions, I may either continue to push for more extreme values or begin to explore positive values to further understand the utility functions of the other parties.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "f2213c5f-9fad-4d63-8a88-4ec34cf4f2f1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to find a balance by moving slightly closer to zero, which might be more comfortable for all parties involved.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will analyze the reactions to this proposal. If there's resistance to moving closer to zero, I might reassess and consider an alternative strategy, such as proposing a smaller increment or exploring the implications of staying at a lower value to better understand the other parties' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "f2213c5f-9fad-4d63-8a88-4ec34cf4f2f1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aligns with Critic C's previous proposal and allows for further exploration of negative values, which may provide insight into the other parties' utility functions. By moving to -4, we can assess the group's comfort with more decisive positions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the responses to this proposal, particularly noting whether there's resistance or acceptance of moving further away from 0. Based on the reactions, I may either continue to push for more extreme values or begin to explore minimal compromises to better understand the utility functions of the other parties.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "f2213c5f-9fad-4d63-8a88-4ec34cf4f2f1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nThis adjustment continues the exploration of negative values, further assessing the group's comfort with more decisive positions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly noting whether there's resistance or acceptance of moving further away from 0, and adjust my strategy to either continue pushing for more extreme values or explore positive values to further understand the other parties' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "f2213c5f-9fad-4d63-8a88-4ec34cf4f2f1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll gauge the reactions to this proposal, observing whether the other parties accept or resist moving closer to 0. Based on their responses, I may either continue to push for less negative values or reassess my strategy to explore alternative compromises.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "f2213c5f-9fad-4d63-8a88-4ec34cf4f2f1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a balance by moving slightly closer to zero, which might be more comfortable for all parties involved. We could move slightly higher to explore the group's comfort with less negative values.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "f2213c5f-9fad-4d63-8a88-4ec34cf4f2f1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "f2213c5f-9fad-4d63-8a88-4ec34cf4f2f1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis proposal explores a small positive value to gauge the group's reaction, considering the recent movements towards zero and the potential for symmetric ut